author ai
group gui
note Keeping the open window honest about what is on disk without ever stalling a frame. A watcher thread holds the indexed files' modification times and compares them against the disk once a second, so the main thread never stats the tree; it sends one message when something moved and then waits for the refreshed list. The frame itself only checks the map's directory, through MapStore::stamp: a map written by the CLI is reloaded silently when there is nothing unsaved, and with unsaved edits it is left alone and the status says so once, because saving would overwrite it. A map on disk that does not read, a merge conflict in it for instance, keeps the one in memory and stops saves until it reads. A changed source file starts a rebuild on a runtime::Job; the index in use is untouched until the new one arrives, and taking it invalidates every SymbolId and FileId in the Model - so the focused symbol, the kept peek, the current file and what the graph shows are carried across by (file path, symbol name) identity and the map's anchors are re-resolved. Neither kind of reload is a navigation: the selection is kept where the new map still supports it and the graph's camera does not move. A deleted file reads as changed and the rebuild drops it; a created file is not noticed until some other file changes.

