note The carry-over, used by every index change (a re-index here, merged server answers in poll_backend). Symbol and file ids do not survive a new index, so the focused symbol, the kept peek (a symbol or a line) and the current file are saved as (path, symbol name) keys first and looked up again after, the graph saves and restores what it shows the same way, and the map's anchors and the comments' anchors are re-resolved, then refresh_wizard rebuilds an open wizard's rows and pending edit against the new index. Hovers are forgotten and the drawn grids dropped, since both were keyed on the old index. Anything whose symbol is gone is simply dropped.

