note The source half, on its own thread (a runtime::service): it is handed the stamps of every index the main thread builds and compares them against the disk once a second, so a 500-file tree is stat'ed off the main thread. It reports a change once and then blocks until the refreshed list arrives, which is how one edit does not become a message every second while the rebuild runs. A file that disappeared counts as changed; one that appeared is invisible to it, since it is not in the list.

