note The reload keeps as much of the reading position as the new map still supports: the tour by name, the selected step when the step at that index still has the same anchor (file, symbol and offsets), and a tour's step views when its step count is unchanged. Tours are matched by name throughout, so a tour added or removed by the agent does not shift another tour's state onto the wrong rows. An open wizard's rows and pending edit are rebuilt against the reloaded map (refresh_wizard). An Err, worded by cli's Failure::Load, leaves the window's map as it was; poll_disk then marks the disk Broken, so a save cannot write over files that did not read.

